    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Daily Meeting Research Brief\n\nThis workflow researches your meeting attendees every morning and sends you a comprehensive brief via Slack DM.\n\n### What it does\n1. **6 AM Trigger**: Runs every weekday morning\n2. **Calendar Scan**: Fetches today's meetings from Google Calendar\n3. **AI Research**: For each external meeting:\n   - Searches web via Firecrawl\n   - Checks Gmail for past interactions\n   - Looks up contacts in Attio CRM\n   - Researches companies via Apollo.io\n4. **Brief Generation**: Creates scannable meeting prep\n5. **Slack DM**: Sends brief directly to you\n\n### Required Credentials (configure in n8n)\n- **Google Calendar OAuth2** - for calendar access\n- **Gmail OAuth2** - for email history search\n- **Slack OAuth2** - for sending DM\n- **OpenRouter API** - for AI processing\n- **Firecrawl API** - HTTP Header Auth (key: Authorization, value: Bearer YOUR_KEY)\n- **Attio API** - HTTP Bearer Auth with your API key\n- **Apollo.io API** - HTTP Header Auth (key: X-Api-Key, value: YOUR_KEY)\n\n### Setup Steps\n1. Configure all credentials above\n2. Update 'User Configuration' node with your email\n3. Select your calendar in 'Get Today's Meetings' node\n4. Set your Slack user ID in both Slack nodes\n5. Test with Manual Trigger first\n6. Activate workflow when ready",
        "height": 850,
        "width": 650,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "sticky-docs",
      "name": "Workflow Documentation",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
