    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Create a scannable meeting brief for my {{ $json.output.length }} meetings today.\n\nIMPORTANT: Format using Slack mrkdwn syntax (NOT standard markdown):\n- Use *bold* for emphasis (single asterisks)\n- Use _italic_ for secondary emphasis (underscores)\n- Use `code` for technical terms\n- NO headers with # (Slack doesn't support them)\n- NO **double asterisks**\n- Add a BLANK LINE between each field for readability\n\nFor EACH meeting, use this EXACT format with blank lines between fields:\n\n*[TIME] Meeting Title*\n\n_Who:_ Name, Company/Role\n\n_Purpose:_ 2-3 sentences on why this meeting matters\n\n_Key Context:_ 1-2 critical facts about them/their company\n\n_Action:_ Your main goal for this meeting\n\n_Watch For:_ One thing to pay attention to\n\n---\n\nRules:\n- The meeting title line MUST be bold using *asterisks*\n- Add a blank line after EVERY field (Who, Purpose, Key Context, Action, Watch For)\n- Be extremely concise and actionable\n- No introductions or conclusions\n- Focus on intelligence that helps me prepare\n- Separate meetings with a divider line (---)\n\nMeeting research data:\n{{ $json.output.map((m, i) => `\\n=== MEETING ${i + 1} ===\\n${JSON.stringify(m, null, 2)}\\n`).join('\\n') }}",
        "batching": {}
      },
